<!-- ════════════════════════════════════════ HEADER ════════════════════════════════════════ -->
<div class="page-header">
  <div class="badge">iplus Living — Technical Reference</div>
  <h1>Access Controller — How It Works</h1>
  <p>How iplus integrates with MQTT-based video intercom &amp; door access controllers (Fermax "Meet" panels) for facial recognition entry, remote door opening, and visitor QR access.</p>
</div>

<div class="container">

  <!-- ═══ WHAT IS IT ═══ -->
  <div class="section-label">Overview</div>
  <h2>What is the Access Controller (Meet) Module?</h2>

  <div class="card">
    <p style="font-size:15px; margin-bottom:20px;">
      The <strong>Access Controller</strong> module — internally called <strong>"Meet" / "Meet FR"</strong> — connects iplus to physical <strong>video intercom panels</strong> (Fermax hardware) installed at building entrances, lift lobbies, and gates. Communication happens over an <strong>MQTT broker</strong>, enabling real-time door commands, facial recognition sync, and access events.
    </p>
    <div class="what-grid">
      <div class="what-item">
        <div class="icon">📡</div>
        <div>
          <h3>MQTT is the transport</h3>
          <p>iplus and the door panel both connect to a shared MQTT broker. Commands and events flow as JSON messages over MQTT topics, not HTTP polling.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="what-item">
        <div class="icon">🧑‍🤝‍🧑</div>
        <div>
          <h3>Faces are the access credential</h3>
          <p>Residents, staff, and visitors get their face data ("FEA" feature files) synced to the panel. The panel recognises faces locally and opens the door.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="what-item">
        <div class="icon">🔓</div>
        <div>
          <h3>Remote door open from the app</h3>
          <p>Residents can remotely unlock a door/gate/lift directly from the iplus mobile app — iplus sends a "remoteOpen" command via MQTT to the panel.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="what-item">
        <div class="icon">⏰</div>
        <div>
          <h3>Time-bound access</h3>
          <p>Every access grant (resident, staff, visitor) has a time zone / schedule — access can be 24/7, business hours only, or a specific date range.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="section-divider"></div>

  <!-- ═══ WHO IS INVOLVED ═══ -->
  <div class="section-label">Actors</div>
  <h2>Who is Involved?</h2>

  <div class="card">
    <div class="actors-grid">
      <div class="actor-card ac-purple">
        <div class="icon">🚪</div>
        <h3>Meet Panel (Hardware)</h3>
        <p>Fermax video intercom installed at gates, lobbies, lifts. Connects to the MQTT broker, stores synced faces, recognises visitors, sends heartbeats and access events.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="actor-card ac-blue">
        <div class="icon">📡</div>
        <h3>MQTT Broker</h3>
        <p>Central message bus (<code style="font-size:12px;">3.0.204.184:1883</code>) that relays commands from iplus to panels and events from panels back to iplus.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="actor-card ac-green">
        <div class="icon">🏠</div>
        <h3>Resident</h3>
        <p>Sees panel list in the app, can remotely open doors, generates QR codes for guests, and gets notified when a visitor is recognised at the door.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="actor-card ac-amber">
        <div class="icon">👤</div>
        <h3>Visitor</h3>
        <p>Granted time-limited access via QR code or face sync. Recognised by the panel during their valid access window only.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="actor-card ac-red">
        <div class="icon">🛡️</div>
        <h3>Staff</h3>
        <p>Granted recurring access based on shift schedules / access groups (e.g., cleaners, technicians) configured per condo.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="actor-card ac-gray">
        <div class="icon">🏢</div>
        <h3>Property Management</h3>
        <p>Registers panels, sets access time zones &amp; holidays, manages access groups, and receives heartbeat-failure alerts.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="section-divider"></div>

  <!-- ═══ STEP BY STEP FLOW ═══ -->
  <div class="section-label">End-to-End Flow</div>
  <h2>How Access is Granted — Step by Step</h2>

  <div class="card">
    <div class="flow">

      <!-- STEP 1 -->
      <div class="flow-step">
        <div class="flow-left">
          <div class="step-circle" style="background:var(--purple);">1</div>
          <div class="step-line"></div>
        </div>
        <div class="flow-body">
          <div class="title">Panel is registered in iplus</div>
          <div class="desc">Property management registers each physical door/intercom panel against the condo, either one-by-one or via bulk CSV import.</div>
          <div class="detail-box">
            Backend: <code>backend/controllers/MqttPanelController.php</code><br/>
            Table: <code>meet_fr_panel</code> — stores <code>mqtt_id</code> (subscription ID), <code>panel_name</code>, <code>panel_description</code>, mapping to block/unit<br/>
            CSV import: "Panel ID (Subscription ID)", "Panel Name", "Panel Description"
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- STEP 2 -->
      <div class="flow-step">
        <div class="flow-left">
          <div class="step-circle" style="background:var(--purple);">2</div>
          <div class="step-line"></div>
        </div>
        <div class="flow-body">
          <div class="title">Access groups &amp; time zones are configured</div>
          <div class="desc">Management defines WHO can access WHICH panels, and WHEN.</div>
          <div class="detail-box">
            <code>meet_fr_time_zone</code> — defines schedules (e.g. "24/7", "Weekdays 9-5")<br/>
            <code>meet_fr_time_zone_interval_link</code> — specific day/time ranges + holidays<br/>
            <code>meet_fr_unit_mapping</code> — which units/residents can access which panels<br/>
            <code>meet_fr_visitor_mapping</code> / <code>meet_fr_staff_access_group</code> — visitor &amp; staff access rules<br/>
            <code>common_access_group</code> — unified access groups (type=4 for Meet FR)
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- STEP 3 -->
      <div class="flow-step">
        <div class="flow-left">
          <div class="step-circle" style="background:var(--purple);">3</div>
          <div class="step-line"></div>
        </div>
        <div class="flow-body">
          <div class="title">Face is captured and a "FEA" feature file is created</div>
          <div class="desc">When a resident, staff member, or visitor is approved for access, their photo is processed into a facial-recognition feature file.</div>
          <div class="detail-box">
            Component: <code>CommonComponent::createFeaFile()</code><br/>
            Calls SP: <code>meet_fr_mqtt_request_response</code><br/>
            Stored in: <code>meet_fr_fea</code> (feature path + status)<br/>
            Time-range aware — only created if access is currently within the valid date/time window
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- STEP 4 -->
      <div class="flow-step">
        <div class="flow-left">
          <div class="step-circle" style="background:var(--purple);">4</div>
          <div class="step-line"></div>
        </div>
        <div class="flow-body">
          <div class="title">iplus pushes "syncFace" command via MQTT</div>
          <div class="desc">The face feature file is sent to the relevant panel(s) so the device can recognise this person locally — even if offline.</div>
          <div class="detail-box">
            Direction: <span class="tag tag-purple">iplus → MQTT Broker → Panel</span><br/>
            Action: <code>syncFace</code><br/>
            Logged in: <code>meet_fr_mqtt_call</code> (request payload, token, attempt count)<br/>
            Component: <code>CommonComponent::syncFace()</code> → <code>callMqtt()</code>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- STEP 5 -->
      <div class="flow-step">
        <div class="flow-left">
          <div class="step-circle" style="background:var(--green);">5</div>
          <div class="step-line"></div>
        </div>
        <div class="flow-body">
          <div class="title">Panel responds with sync confirmation</div>
          <div class="desc">The panel acknowledges that the face has been stored on-device.</div>
          <div class="detail-box">
            Logged in: <code>meet_fr_mqtt_call_response</code><br/>
            Fields: device response, failure ID, receive code<br/>
            <code>token_status</code>: 1=Valid, 2=Used &nbsp;|&nbsp; <code>response_status</code>: HTTP-style code (200=Success, 202=Processing, 404=Not Found)
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- STEP 6 -->
      <div class="flow-step">
        <div class="flow-left">
          <div class="step-circle" style="background:var(--green);">6</div>
          <div class="step-line"></div>
        </div>
        <div class="flow-body">
          <div class="title">Person arrives — panel recognises them</div>
          <div class="desc">The visitor/resident/staff member walks up to the panel. Facial recognition runs locally on the device.</div>
          <div class="detail-box">
            Panel sends MQTT event: <code>passEvent</code><br/>
            Logged in: <code>meet_fr_mqtt_device_response</code><br/>
            <code>code_status</code>: <span class="tag tag-green">0 = Success</span> &nbsp; <span class="tag tag-red">501–507 = Recognition errors</span> &nbsp; <span class="tag tag-amber">10000 = Unknown</span><br/>
            On success → door opens automatically
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- STEP 7 -->
      <div class="flow-step">
        <div class="flow-left">
          <div class="step-circle" style="background:var(--green);">7</div>
          <div class="step-line"></div>
        </div>
        <div class="flow-body">
          <div class="title">Resident gets a "visitor at door" notification</div>
          <div class="desc">If the recognised face belongs to a visitor with active access, the resident who invited them is notified.</div>
          <div class="detail-box">
            SP: <code>meet_panel_remote_open_list</code> — finds eligible <code>passEvent</code> rows where <code>push_used = 0</code> and <code>code_status = 0</code><br/>
            Insert into: <code>meet_fr_mqtt_remote_push</code><br/>
            Notification frequency configurable: <code>notification_to_resident_type</code> = Every time / First per day / Once only
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- STEP 8 -->
      <div class="flow-step">
        <div class="flow-left">
          <div class="step-circle" style="background:var(--blue);">8</div>
          <div class="step-line"></div>
        </div>
        <div class="flow-body">
          <div class="title">Resident remotely opens the door (alternative path)</div>
          <div class="desc">Instead of (or in addition to) face recognition, the resident can tap "Open Door" in the app for a remote unlock.</div>
          <div class="detail-box">
            API: <code>POST /apiver6/intercom/panelrelay</code> (param: <code>panel_number</code>)<br/>
            Returns relay list / DTMF tones, then triggers:<br/>
            Component: <code>CommonComponent::remoteOpen()</code> → MQTT action <code>remoteOpen</code><br/>
            Direction: <span class="tag tag-purple">App → iplus → MQTT Broker → Panel</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- STEP 9 -->
      <div class="flow-step">
        <div class="flow-left">
          <div class="step-circle" style="background:var(--amber);">9</div>
          <div class="step-line"></div>
        </div>
        <div class="flow-body">
          <div class="title">Access expires → face is removed</div>
          <div class="desc">When a visitor pass expires or staff access is revoked, the face is deleted from the panel automatically.</div>
          <div class="detail-box">
            Component: <code>CommonComponent::removeFeaFile()</code><br/>
            MQTT action: <code>deleteFace</code> (single face) or <code>clearFace</code> (clear entire device — admin/emergency action)<br/>
            Field: <code>remove_face_id</code> tracks which face was removed
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- STEP 10 -->
